From: VLC Juxtopposed contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Wake every eligible waiter after the last reader exits

Readers and writers share a condition variable. A priority writer can be
waiting alongside readers that must give way. Waking only one waiter can
choose an ineligible reader and leave the writer asleep with no remaining
lock owner to notify it. Let every waiter recheck its predicate.

--- a/src/utils/SWMRLock.cpp
+++ b/src/utils/SWMRLock.cpp
@@ -54,7 +54,11 @@ void SWMRLock::unlock_read()
     std::unique_lock<compat::Mutex> lock( m_lock );
     --m_nbReader;
     if ( m_nbReader == 0 && m_nbWriterWaiting > 0 )
-        m_cond.notify_one();
+        // Readers and writers share this condition variable. A reader
+        // blocked by a priority writer cannot proceed if notify_one()
+        // wakes it instead of that writer; no lock owner remains to wake
+        // the eligible writer. Every waiter must recheck its predicate.
+        m_cond.notify_all();
 }

 void SWMRLock::lock_write()
